{"resourceIdentifier":"1085","resourceName":"EcoPlanet Bamboo Central America - Reforestation Project","description":"This verified project utilizes a species of indigenous bamboo, Guadua aculeata, for the regeneration of degraded pasture lands on the Atlantic coast of Nicaragua. The project area was once primary tropical forest but underwent extreme deforestation in the 1970s and 1980s. The project has a total area of 3,199.1 hectares of degraded land across three farms, of which 2,361.4 hectares have been planted with bamboo. The project is designed to provide a sustainable alternative fiber, thereby further reducing pressure on natural forests, while generating significant carbon removals and positive social and environmental impact.\r\n\r\nThe project was validated in 2013 and verified in 2015. The most recent verification event occurred in 2020-2021. \r\n\r\nThe project was validated to CCBA and received gold level validation, however no verification of CCBA has occurred.","location":{"latitude":12.280380,"longitude":85.275137},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1085"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Southern Atlantic Autonomous Region (RAAS)"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"EcoPlanet Bamboo Group, LLC"},{"type":"string","value":"DE, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"+254-721-999-604"},{"type":"string","value":"crebelo@ecoplanetbamboo.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1085"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1085"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"40815"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":24473}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","val